From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Mills <travismills82@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 00:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] backup: exclude regeneratable nandswap data from FBE backup

The device-level TW_BACKUP_EXCLUSIONS entry does not prevent the Android 16
FBE backup path from traversing /data/nandswap. The directory is regenerated
by Android and its vendor-specific fscrypt policy cannot be serialized by
TWRP, producing a policy lookup failure during otherwise successful backups.

Add /data/nandswap directly to the FBE exclusion object alongside cache,
per_boot, and GSI data so size calculation and tar generation both skip it.
---
 partition.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/partition.cpp b/partition.cpp
index 69f7cb4c..00000000 100644
--- a/partition.cpp
+++ b/partition.cpp
@@ -803,6 +803,7 @@ bool TWPartition::Decrypt_FBE_DE() {
 	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/system_de/0/spblob");  // contains data needed to decrypt synthetic password
 	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/system/users/0/gatekeeper.password.key");
 	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/system/users/0/gatekeeper.pattern.key");
+	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/nandswap"); // regenerated by Android; vendor fscrypt policy is not restorable
 	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/cache");
 	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/per_boot"); // removed each boot by init
 	ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/gsi"); // cow devices
